<p><%= link_to "&larr; All runs".html_safe, admin_runs_path %></p>

<h1>Run #<%= @run.id %></h1>

<dl>
  <dt>When</dt>
  <dd><%= @run.created_at %></dd>

  <dt>Agent</dt>
  <dd><%= @run.agent_slug %> &middot; <%= @run.subject_type %>#<%= @run.subject_id %></dd>

  <dt>Trigger</dt>
  <dd><%= @run.trigger %></dd>

  <dt>Status</dt>
  <dd><%= @run.status %><%= " (#{@run.error_class})" if @run.error_class %></dd>

  <dt>Model</dt>
  <dd><%= @run.model || "—" %> &middot; <%= @run.total_tokens %> tokens</dd>

  <dt>Snapshot</dt>
  <dd><code><%= @run.snapshot_digest %></code></dd>

  <dt>Memories injected</dt>
  <dd><%= @run.memory_ids.any? ? @run.memory_ids.join(", ") : "none" %></dd>
</dl>

<h2>Rules injected <small>(engine — evidence)</small></h2>

<p>
  Written by the engine from the rule set it rendered into the prompt, pinned at
  the version each rule was then. This is evidence of what the agent
  <strong>was told</strong>.
</p>

<% if @run.rules.any? %>
  <ul>
    <% @run.injected_rule_texts.each do |text| %>
      <li><%= text %></li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
<% else %>
  <p><em>No rules were in force for this run.</em></p>
<% end %>

<h2>Rules the agent <em>claims</em> it applied <small>(unverified)</small></h2>

<p>
  A line the model wrote in its own reply. It is <strong>not</strong> proof any of
  these rules was followed — a model has been observed contradicting a rule while
  sincerely citing it, and that turn records exactly like a compliant one.
</p>

<p>
  <% if @run.rule_ids_applied.any? %>
    <%= @run.rule_ids_applied.join(", ") %> — <em>claimed, not verified</em>
  <% else %>
    <em>Nothing cited.</em>
  <% end %>
</p>

<% if @run.unknown_citations? %>
  <p><strong>Cited but never injected: <%= @run.unknown_rule_ids.join(", ") %>.</strong>
    An id the model produced that was not in its prompt — invented, or from a scope
    it should never have seen.</p>
<% end %>

<h2>
  <%= @run.trigger == "proactive" ? "What set the agent off" : "What the customer asked" %>
</h2>

<p>
  <%= if @run.trigger == "proactive"
        "There was no inbound question: this turn was opened by the engine, and this " \
        "is the instruction it opened with."
      else
        "The other half of the turn. A reply read on its own is thin evidence — the " \
        "same sentence is unremarkable or alarming depending on what it was answering."
      end %>
</p>

<% if (prompt = @run.prompt_text) %>
  <%# Escaped as carefully as the reply below. A customer can type markup too. %>
  <pre class="concierge-reply"><%= prompt %></pre>
<% else %>
  <p>
    <em>
      <% case @run.prompt_unavailable_reason %>
      <% when :no_host_chat %>
        No host chat was recorded for this run, so there is no question to read.
      <% when :not_persisted %>
        No customer message was persisted for this turn, so there is nothing to read
        back. Runs recorded before the engine wrote the customer's turn down all
        read this way, as does any host whose <code>chat_factory</code> keeps no
        messages.
      <% else %>
        The host has pruned this message (chat #<%= @run.chat_id %>,
        message #<%= @run.prompt_message_id %>). Retention of customer conversations
        is the host's call, not the engine's.
      <% end %>
    </em>
  </p>
<% end %>

<h2>What the agent actually said</h2>

<p>
  The check the engine cannot perform. Read this against the claim above, and
  against the question above that: a rule cited and followed and a rule cited and
  contradicted are indistinguishable on every other line of this page.
</p>

<% if (reply = @run.reply_text) %>
  <%# Verbatim and fully escaped. This is untrusted model output on an operator's
      screen: anything that renders it as markup lets a reply put a link, or a
      bolded reassurance, into the very page an auditor is reading it on. %>
  <pre class="concierge-reply"><%= reply %></pre>

  <p>
    <small>
      Read live from the host's own chat tables
      (chat #<%= @run.chat_id %>, message #<%= @run.message_id %>); Concierge keeps a
      pointer, never a copy, so how long these words are retained stays the host's
      decision. This is the <strong>raw</strong> message the model produced — the
      citation line is still on it, because the engine strips that only from the
      reply it hands to a channel, never from the host's record of the turn.
    </small>
  </p>
<% else %>
  <p>
    <em>
      <% case @run.reply_unavailable_reason %>
      <% when :no_host_chat %>
        No host chat was recorded for this run, so there is no message to read.
        The engine opens a conversation for every run now, with or without
        provider credentials — so this is a run recorded before it did, or one
        whose host keeps no chat model at all. Either way this turn's words were
        never written down anywhere Concierge can reach.
      <% when :not_persisted %>
        This run used host chat #<%= @run.chat_id %>, but no assistant message was
        persisted for the turn, so there is nothing to read back.
      <% else %>
        The host has pruned this message (chat #<%= @run.chat_id %>,
        message #<%= @run.message_id %>). Retention of customer conversations is the
        host's call, not the engine's — the link is kept so the gap is visible
        rather than silent.
      <% end %>
    </em>
  </p>

  <p>
    <small>
      With no reply to read, this run's citation <strong>cannot be spot-checked at
      all</strong>. Treat it as unverified, not as compliant.
    </small>
  </p>
<% end %>
